DESCRIPTION:Radio-echo sounding of ice sheets provides key constraints on 
 englacial and subglacial material and thermal conditions. However\, standa
 rd survey configurations have made it difficult to unambiguously resolve p
 roperties such as fine-scale bed geometry\, ice temperature\, and subglaci
 al hydrological conditions and to monitor how these properties evolve over
  time. This work presents a set of low-cost modifications to existing rada
 r systems (using radio frequency-over-fiber) that help address these li\n
 \nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-03 11:59 PST
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
END:VEVENT
