SUMMARY:[Applied Physics/Physics Colloquium] Applied Physics/Physics Collo
 quium: Alexander Maloney - " Wormholes and the Conformal Bootstrap"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T163000
DTSTAMP:20261103T195903Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54373952074964-54373952075989@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: A wormhole is a geometry which connects two widely s
 eparated regions of space-time.  Wormholes are ubiquitous in many theories
  of gravity\, but remain poorly understood.  However\, we can study them u
 sing the "AdS/CFT correspondence\," which relates theories of quantum grav
 ity to conformal field theories (CFTs) in one less dimension.  These CFTs 
 are similar to the gauge theories which describe the fundamental forces of
  particle physics\, as well as to those which describe important statist\n
 \nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-03 11:59 PST
LOCATION:Hewlett Teaching Center
END:VEVENT
